ref=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-5b\" transform=\"translate(575.9375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(666.53125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-69\" transform=\"translate(721.328125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-4e\" transform=\"translate(759.625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-50\" transform=\"translate(819.828125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-5c\" transform=\"translate(843.734375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a5\" transform=\"translate(902.140625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(923.546875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-4d\" transform=\"translate(978.34375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-6c\" transform=\"translate(1016.25 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-48\" transform=\"translate(1053.65625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-69\" transform=\"translate(1111.75 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a5\" transform=\"translate(1150.046875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-66\" transform=\"translate(1171.453125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-4f\" transform=\"translate(1231.15625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(1289.5625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-69\" transform=\"translate(1344.359375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-5b\" transform=\"translate(1382.65625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(1473.25 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-44\" transform=\"translate(1528.046875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-75\" transform=\"translate(1580.953125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a5\" transform=\"translate(1633.953125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-6a\" transform=\"translate(1655.359375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-4f\" transform=\"translate(1706.5625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(1764.96875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-69\" transform=\"translate(1819.765625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-48\" transform=\"translate(1856.765625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a5\" transform=\"translate(1914.859375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-bd\" transform=\"translate(1936.265625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-dd\" transform=\"translate(1964.859375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-be\" transform=\"translate(2025.359375 0)\"/></g></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pc63db1ccdf\"><rect x=\"41.186281\" y=\"27.296\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Retail price and Velisse Skin's margin per unit ($)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Velisse Skin receives 65% of the retail price; the pharmacy keeps 35%.</p> <p>Bottle: $48 × 65% = $31.20 − $18 = <b>$13.20</b>. Refill: $40 × 65% = $26.00 − $11 = <b>$15.00</b>. A refill earns Velisse Skin more than a bottle.</p> <p>A switcher's annual margin: 3.4 × $15.00 = $51.00 vs 3 × $13.20 = $39.60 before: <b>+$11.40</b> each.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> cannibalisation doesn't hurt here; switching customers are worth more.</p>"},{"q":"Calculate the total annual impact.","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Switchers: 61.6k × $11.40 = $0.70M.</p> <p>New customers: 32k × (1 bottle × $13.20 + 2.4 refills × $15.00) = $1.57M.</p> <p>Minus $1.35M of costs: <b>+$0.93M a year</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> worthwhile, and most of the value comes from new customers, but the yearly costs eat most of the gross gain.</p>"},{"q":"How might pharmacies react, and what would you do?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>A pharmacy earns $16.80 on a bottle but $14.00 on a refill: they lose $2.80 each time a customer switches, so they may not stock or promote refills.</p> <p>Matching their $16.80 on every refill needs a 42% share. That cuts Velisse Skin's refill margin to $12.20 and the total gain to about +$0.13M a year: almost nothing.</p> <ul><li>Raise the pharmacy's share on refills only partly, or tie it to refill volume</li><li>Refill-station displays that also bring traffic into the pharmacy</li> <li>Sell refills online too, but avoid undercutting pharmacies on price</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Launch the refill. After the pharmacy's 35% share, Velisse Skin earns more on a refill ($15.00) than on a bottle ($13.20), so switching customers are worth more, and new customers add most of the value: about +$0.93M a year after launch costs. The real risk is pharmacies, which earn $2.80 less per refill. Raise their share on refills only partly (matching them fully would cut the gain to about $0.1M), or tie it to refill volume. Next step: test refill stations in 50 pharmacies for three months.","great":["Works out the margin after the channel's share, not on retail price","Shows cannibalisation is harmless here","Quantifies the new-customer gain","Spots the channel partner's incentive problem and prices the fix"],"id":44,"slug":"velisse-skin"}